      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The original settlement, founded in 1836 by John Ferdon, was first called Williamsport after pioneer Clark Williams before becoming Barrington and Swizzletown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eureka%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Eureka sits in northeastern Greenbush Township, about 30 miles north of Lansing and 40 miles south of Mount Pleasant in Michigan’s Lower Peninsula.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eureka%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Halterman Creek winds through the community, adding a gentle waterway to the town’s rural landscape.",
